The adapter service keeps one loopback listener running for every saved
profile. Each profile is a path on that listener, for example
http://127.0.0.1:8099/cully/mcp. Only that port is used. Other localhost
ports are left alone. MCP clients call the profile URL directly. The daemon
presents that profile's enrolled certificate upstream and forwards the
client's OAuth bearer when the server requires one.

Foreground troubleshooting stays on "adapter proxy".

Usage:
  mcp-runtime adapter service [command]

Available Commands:
  install     Install the user LaunchAgent
  logs        Show recent redacted daemon logs
  profile     Add or remove a daemon profile
  restart     Restart the adapter daemon
  start       Start the adapter daemon
  status      Show daemon and profile status
  stop        Stop the adapter daemon
  uninstall   Remove the LaunchAgent and stop the managed daemon

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for service

Global Flags:
      --debug   Enable debug mode with structured error logging

Use "mcp-runtime adapter service [command] --help" for more information about a command.
